6,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[-2,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,-2,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[8,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,8,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[-2,8,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,-2,8,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[-2,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,-2,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[8,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,8,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[-2,8,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4],[6,-2,8,0,-7,1,3,10,-9,4]]},{"args":[[-4,9,10,-9,-2]],"expected":[[],[-4],[9],[-4,9],[10],[-4,10],[9,10],[-4,9,10],[-9],[-4,-9],[9,-9],[-4,9,-9],[10,-9],[-4,10,-9],[9,10,-9],[-4,9,10,-9],[-2],[-4,-2],[9,-2],[-4,9,-2],[10,-2],[-4,10,-2],[9,10,-2],[-4,9,10,-2],[-9,-2],[-4,-9,-2],[9,-9,-2],[-4,9,-9,-2],[10,-9,-2],[-4,10,-9,-2],[9,10,-9,-2],[-4,9,10,-9,-2]]},{"args":[[8]],"expected":[[],[8]]},{"args":[[0,-2]],"expected":[[],[0],[-2],[0,-2]]},{"args":[[8]],"expected":[[],[8]]},{"args":[[-9,-6]],"expected":[[],[-9],[-6],[-9,-6]]},{"args":[[7,2,10,0,4]],"expected":[[],[7],[2],[7,2],[10],[7,10],[2,10],[7,2,10],[0],[7,0],[2,0],[7,2,0],[10,0],[7,10,0],[2,10,0],[7,2,10,0],[4],[7,4],[2,4],[7,2,4],[10,4],[7,10,4],[2,10,4],[7,2,10,4],[0,4],[7,0,4],[2,0,4],[7,2,0,4],[10,0,4],[7,10,0,4],[2,10,0,4],[7,2,10,0,4]]},{"args":[[5,-5,4,-4]],"expected":[[],[5],[-5],[5,-5],[4],[5,4],[-5,4],[5,-5,4],[-4],[5,-4],[-5,-4],[5,-5,-4],[4,-4],[5,4,-4],[-5,4,-4],[5,-5,4,-4]]},{"args":[[5,-4,3,6,-3]],"expected":[[],[5],[-4],[5,-4],[3],[5,3],[-4,3],[5,-4,3],[6],[5,6],[-4,6],[5,-4,6],[3,6],[5,3,6],[-4,3,6],[5,-4,3,6],[-3],[5,-3],[-4,-3],[5,-4,-3],[3,-3],[5,3,-3],[-4,3,-3],[5,-4,3,-3],[6,-3],[5,6,-3],[-4,6,-3],[5,-4,6,-3],[3,6,-3],[5,3,6,-3],[-4,3,6,-3],[5,-4,3,6,-3]]},{"args":[[6,-6,-4,0,-7,9]],"expected":[[],[6],[-6],[6,-6],[-4],[6,-4],[-6,-4],[6,-6,-4],[0],[6,0],[-6,0],[6,-6,0],[-4,0],[6,-4,0],[-6,-4,0],[6,-6,-4,0],[-7],[6,-7],[-6,-7],[6,-6,-7],[-4,-7],[6,-4,-7],[-6,-4,-7],[6,-6,-4,-7],[0,-7],[6,0,-7],[-6,0,-7],[6,-6,0,-7],[-4,0,-7],[6,-4,0,-7],[-6,-4,0,-7],[6,-6,-4,0,-7],[9],[6,9],[-6,9],[6,-6,9],[-4,9],[6,-4,9],[-6,-4,9],[6,-6,-4,9],[0,9],[6,0,9],[-6,0,9],[6,-6,0,9],[-4,0,9],[6,-4,0,9],[-6,-4,0,9],[6,-6,-4,0,9],[-7,9],[6,-7,9],[-6,-7,9],[6,-6,-7,9],[-4,-7,9],[6,-4,-7,9],[-6,-4,-7,9],[6,-6,-4,-7,9],[0,-7,9],[6,0,-7,9],[-6,0,-7,9],[6,-6,0,-7,9],[-4,0,-7,9],[6,-4,0,-7,9],[-6,-4,0,-7,9],[6,-6,-4,0,-7,9]]},{"args":[[-5,1,9]],"expected":[[],[-5],[1],[-5,1],[9],[-5,9],[1,9],[-5,1,9]]}],"gen":"(r, big) => [r.distinct(big ? 10 : r.int(1, 6), -10, 10)]","hints":["Walk through the numbers one at a time. For each one there are exactly two choices. How many subsets does that give?","Build subsets with one shared list: add a number, go deeper, then remove it again before trying the next number. Every list you hold along the way is a subset.","Recurse with a start index. Record a copy of the current list, then for each i from start onward: push nums[i], recurse with i + 1, pop. Using i + 1 means you only ever add numbers to the right of the last one, so no subset is built twice."],"explain":{"intuition":"<p>Backtracking is a way to list every answer by making one decision at a time. Picture a <b>decision tree</b>. The root is the empty list. Its children add one number each: <code>[7]</code>, <code>[0]</code>, <code>[5]</code>. A node's children add one more number, but only from those to the <b>right</b> of the last number added, so <code>[7]</code> has children <code>[7, 0]</code> and <code>[7, 5]</code>, and <code>[0]</code> has only <code>[0, 5]</code>. Every node of this tree is a different subset, and every subset appears exactly once. The answer is the list of all nodes.</p>\n<p>To walk the tree, keep <b>one</b> shared array <code>cur</code> and repeat three moves at every node: <b>choose</b> (push a number), <b>explore</b> (recurse into that child), <b>un-choose</b> (pop it). The pop puts <code>cur</code> back exactly as it was, so the next sibling starts from a clean state. It is like browsing a folder tree in a sidebar: open a folder, look inside, close it, then open the next one. Every later problem in this group uses this same template. What changes is which children a node has, and when a node counts as an answer.</p>","steps":["Keep the answer list <code>out</code> and one shared array <code>cur</code>.","Define <code>go(start)</code>. First record a <b>copy</b> of <code>cur</code>: every node of the tree is a subset.","For each <code>i</code> from <code>start</code> to the end: <b>choose</b> with <code>cur.push(nums[i])</code>, <b>explore</b> with <code>go(i + 1)</code>, <b>un-choose</b> with <code>cur.pop()</code>.","Call <code>go(0)</code> and return <code>out</code>. It holds 2ⁿ subsets."],"pitfalls":["Recording <code>cur</code> itself instead of a copy. Every entry then points at the same array, which is empty when the search ends.","Forgetting the pop. The next sibling then starts with an extra number left over from the branch before it.","Recursing with <code>go(start + 1)</code> instead of <code>go(i + 1)</code>. Later picks can then go back to the left, which builds <code>[5, 0]</code> as well as <code>[0, 5]</code> and repeats numbers."],"complexity":{"time":"O(n · 2ⁿ): 2ⁿ subsets, each copied in O(n)","space":"O(n) for the recursion and cur, besides the output"}},"solutions":[{"title":"Grow the list one number at a time","idea":"Start with [[]]. For each number, copy every subset found so far and add the number to the copy. The list doubles with each number.","time":"O(n · 2ⁿ)","space":"O(n · 2ⁿ) for the output","ts":"function allSubsets(nums: number[]): number[][] {\n  const out: number[][] = [[]];\n  for (const x of nums) {\n    const size = out.length; // only extend the subsets that existed before x\n    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) out.push([...out[i], x]);\n  }\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def allSubsets(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n        out = [[]]\n        for x in nums:\n            out += [s + [x] for s in out]\n        return out","js":"function allSubsets(nums) {\n  const out = [[]];\n  for (const x of nums) {\n    const size = out.length;\n    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) out.push([...out[i], x]);\n  }\n  return out;\n}"},{"title":"Backtracking: choose, explore, un-choose","idea":"Walk the decision tree with one shared array. Record every node, and only add numbers to the right of the last one added.","time":"O(n · 2ⁿ)","space":"O(n) besides the output","ts":"function allSubsets(nums: number[]): number[][] {\n  const out: number[][] = [];\n  const cur: number[] = [];\n  const go = (start: number): void => {\n    out.push([...cur]); // every node of the tree is a subset\n    for (let i = start; i < nums.length; i++) {\n      cur.push(nums[i]); // choose\n      go(i + 1);         // explore: only numbers to the right\n      cur.pop();         // un-choose\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}","py":"class Solution:\n    def allSubsets(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n        out, cur = [], []\n\n        def go(start: int) -> None:\n            out.append(cur[:])  # every node of the tree is a subset\n            for i in range(start, len(nums)):\n                cur.append(nums[i])  # choose\n                go(i + 1)            # explore: only numbers to the right\n                cur.pop()            # un-choose\n\n        go(0)\n        return out","js":"function allSubsets(nums) {\n  const out = [];\n  const cur = [];\n  const go = (start) => {\n    out.push([...cur]);\n    for (let i = start; i < nums.length; i++) {\n      cur.push(nums[i]);\n      go(i + 1);\n      cur.pop();\n    }\n  };\n  go(0);\n  return out;\n}"}],"followups":["Return only the subsets of exactly k numbers. Where do you record, and what can you prune?","n is now 30. Listing every subset is impossible. What would you return instead, and how would you produce subsets one at a time on demand?"],"related":[],"kind":"function","nEx":3,"nBig":2,"lcTitle":"Subsets","acc":0.0082932476777741,"co":[["Coupang",97,0],["PornHub",87,0],["Bloomberg",70,90],["Wix",70,0],["Amazon",65,90],["Meta",64,30],["Microsoft",59,30],["Agoda",57,180],["Google",52,30],["Uber",52,0],["PayPal",51,0],["TikTok",50,0],["Flipkart",43,0],["Walmart Labs",43,0],["tcs",42,0],["Infosys",39,180],["Oracle",27,0],["Apple",22,0],["Goldman Sachs",21,0]]}